          "correlation_id": "evict-Hyp0thetica1=="
        }
      },
      "notes": "SYNTHETIC / HYPOTHETICAL -- not observed on the live wire. evictor.ex hardcodes `retryable: false` unconditionally today, so the platform has never actually sent `retryable: true`. This case exercises canonical's 'wire field is authoritative' rule in the abstract: band-sdk-python already reads the field (would accept retryable=true here); band-sdk-typescript's disconnectReason.ts hardcodes `retryable: false` regardless of the wire value, so it would silently produce the opposite of this payload's real meaning if the platform ever varied it -- a forward-compatibility concern the plan is recorded here, not a live behavioral bug today (see canonical policy doc).",
      "sdk": {
        "python": {
          "decision": "accept",
